GAM, an intravenous immune globulin (IVIG) product indicated for the treatment of primary humoral immunodeficiency (PI); ASCENIV, an IVIG product for the treatment of PI; and Nabi-HB, a human polyclonal antibody product for the treatment of acute exposure to blood containing Hepatitis B surface antigen and other listed exposures to Hepatitis B. It also develops a pipeline of plasma-derived therapeutics comprising products related to the methods of treatment and prevention of S. pneumonia infection for an immunoglobulin. In addition, the company operates source plasma collection facilities. The company sells its products through independent distributors, drug wholesalers, specialty pharmacies, and other alternate site providers. ADMA Biologics, Inc. was incorporated in 2004 and is headquartered in Ramsey, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Adam S. Grossman | Co-Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 640 people. Revenue per employee of $797K ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 60%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $43K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $31K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["ADMA Biologics Inc is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $3.2B market cap on $510M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +49% over the past three years and +53% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +57.3pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 29% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 20-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 36%.","The business throws off $28M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.34\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","Accruals are elevated at +15.5% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 27\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 4.3\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 33% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.33128082995788904},{"text":"Accruals elevated at +15.5% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.6M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2615286.48},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 26% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 38% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ADMA Biologics (ADMA) Stock May Trade Below Fair Value On Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-adma/adma-biologics/news/adma-biologics-adma-stock-may-trade-below-fair-value-on-earn","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795745657.083,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.964,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Kaitlin M. Kestenberg-Messina Sells 30,000 Shares of ADMA Biologics at $13.87 Each","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/kaitlin-m-kestenberg-messina-sells-30000-shares-of-adma-biologics-at-1387-each","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795659061.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Adma Biologics Inc (ADMA) Affects Rotational Strate